<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- UMW_Pointed. Point shape — a fine needle that slips past armor and bone to find the organs.
       IDENTITY (reshaped 2026-07-27): the trait's lever is WHERE the wound lands, not how big it is —
       a MeleeDamageConversionExtension reroutes the base Stab hit to UMW_Stab_Deep, raising
       stabChanceOfForcedInternal 0.6 -> 0.85 (the def carries the worked mechanics and sizing). The
       damage/AP side is a mild rider, not the point: statFactor x1.1 on MeleeWeapon_DamageMultiplier
       (damage AND armor pen — both ride the one stat; the coupling is kept deliberately, as a finer
       point genuinely drives deeper, unlike UMW_HeadWeighted whose incidental AP we neutralize).
       Reshape rationale: the roster already leans on damage-vs-AP factor tradeoffs (HeadWeighted,
       Counterweighted, Studded, Razored); the earlier x1.2-with-malus shape made NeedlePoint a
       me-too stat trait. Organ-seeking is an untouched axis, is literally the "drives deeper"
       fiction, and differentiates the Point family: raw armor answer (ArmorSpike), attrition
       bleeding (Barbed), vitals-seeking lethality (this) — the kill-weapon mirror of Opiated's
       capture coating. The conversion only touches Stab-capacity swings, so the spear and knife are
       its prime carriers; a longsword or gladius converts only its point-tool swings.

       VEHICLE for the malus: trait-level equippedStatOffsets, made live for our defs by
       StatWorker_UniqueTraitStatOffsets_Patch (the patch header carries the decompile audit and the
       raw-units/display rules); shows as the weapon's own "Relevant gear" line in the wielder's
       MeleeHitChance breakdown. Replaced the former UMW_NeedlePointGrip equipped hediff.

       TUNING: MeleeHitChance offsets are RAW pre-curve units; the curve ((0,0.50) (10,0.80)
       (20,0.90)) prices -1 at 3pp of hit chance below the raw-10 knot and 1pp above — unforgiving
       to whoever hasn't mastered it, without maiming them (an earlier -2 ate half of the then-x1.2
       buff below the knot; softened in the same pass that reshaped the identity). Stat-side net is
       now modest (x1.1 by hit ratio: +3% at skill 0, +5-6% mid, +8-9% high); the organ-seeking is
       the payload. MV 70: above HighPowerRounds' 60 (whose stat package the rider alone no longer
       matches), below ParalyticArrows' 80 / HollowPoint's 85 — lethality priced like a premium
       payload, discounted for the hit-chance cost. cf. Brawler +4, the nearest Core offset to
       MeleeHitChance. -->
  <WeaponTraitDef>
    <defName>UMW_NeedlePoint</defName>
    <label>needle point</label>
    <description>Tapered to a fine needle, the point drives deep beneath bone and muscle, seeking the organs within. The slender point is harder to land cleanly.</description>
    <commonality>1</commonality>
    <weaponCategory>UMW_Pointed</weaponCategory>
    <exclusionTags>
      <li>Point</li>
    </exclusionTags>
    <statOffsets>
      <MarketValue>70</MarketValue> <!-- between HighPowerRounds 60 and ParalyticArrows 80; see header -->
    </statOffsets>
    <statFactors>
      <MeleeWeapon_DamageMultiplier>1.1</MeleeWeapon_DamageMultiplier>
    </statFactors>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <MeleeHitChance>-1</MeleeHitChance> <!-- raw, pre-curve: -3pp below melee 10, -1pp above; see header -->
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <traitAdjectives>
      <li>needle</li>
      <li>needling</li>
      <li>hypodermic</li>
    </traitAdjectives>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.MeleeDamageConversionExtension">
        <conversions>
          <li>
            <from>Stab</from>
            <to>UMW_Stab_Deep</to>
          </li>
        </conversions>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </WeaponTraitDef>

</Defs>
